ef=\"http://www.magiceyetubes.com/\" id=\"mwASo\">Wealth of information on the magic eye</a></li>\n<li id=\"mwASs\"><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://www.solorb.com/elect/misc/magiceye/\" id=\"mwASw\">fluorescent indicator tube photos, pinouts and schematics</a></li>\n<li id=\"mwAS0\"><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20120417004309/http://home.comcast.net/~jlrmsousa/precise_db_monitoring_with_eye_tubes_november_2006_audioxpress_joe_sousa2667.pdf\" id=\"mwAS4\">Precise dB measurements with eye tubes</a></li>\n<li id=\"mwAS8\"><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"http://www.radiomuseum.org/forum/dm70_operation.html\" id=\"mwATA\">How the DM70 operates</a></li>\n<li id=\"mwATE\"><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20140814161420/http://www.hscott.net/magic-eye-tubes/\" id=\"mwATI\">Video demonstration and explanation</a></li>\n<li id=\"mwATM\"><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://lampes-et-tubes.info/ti/ti014.php\" id=\"mwATQ\">Tunograph</a>, first introduced in 1933 (<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"http://www.mif.pg.gda.pl/homepages/frank/sheets/156/t/TUNOGRAPH.pdf\" id=\"mwATU\">data sheet</a>)</li></ul> </section>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.codfw.main‐7fc8f7ffc6‐r4nvn\nCached time: 20260827191620\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Citation/CS1 (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, show‐toc, use‐parsoid]\nCPU time usage: 0.584 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.711 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1984/1000000\nRevision size: 12333/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 76422/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 2854/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 12/100\nExpensive parser function count: 4/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27863/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.083/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 4996635/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 1/500\n-